       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like it could be an error.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That's twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per administration. At this dose the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max IR dose)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that it's a confirmed intentional dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
